  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility study of a 300 MW Wind Project in Karnataka in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, which is located in the State of Karnataka, India, has a capacity of 300 MW and is expected to produce 1,100 GWh of electricity annually. The agreement is under Norad&apos;s Enterprise for Development Scheme (EDFJ). 

Among others, Norad&#x2019;s support covers technical and legal feasibility studies, lenders technical and legal due diligence, establishment of project management structures and social and Environmental impact assessments.</narrative>
  </description>
